      "reviewed": true,
      "translation": "The Blessed Lord said: The wise understand renunciation as the giving up of desire-driven actions; the discerning call relinquishment the giving up of the fruits of all actions. Śrīdhara explains that, until knowledge is steady, necessary duties are still performed for purification while their fruits are relinquished; complete cessation of action arises later with firm realization.",
