      "reviewed": true,
      "translation": "Some thoughtful people say that all action should be abandoned as defective; others say that the actions of sacrifice, charity, and austerity should not be abandoned. Śrīdhara presents the first view as grounded in the binding defects of action, and the second as maintaining that prescribed duties remain necessary.",
