    "15": {
      "reviewed": true,
      "translation": "He states that these alone are the causes of all action, with the verse beginning ‘śarīra.’ Action being undertaken by the five already stated is subsumed within just three; thus it is said ‘by body, speech, and mind,’ because action is well known as threefold—bodily, verbal, and mental. Whatever action, righteous or unrighteous, a man performs by the body and the others, these five are the causes of all that action.",
